(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #112 / LANGUAGE.md 2811-2820, "Conditional `value`
 returns work" - the exact example the manual gives, pinned verbatim.
 Every branch fires here (v is a number in one call, not in the other),
 so this does not itself exercise the fall-off path - #634 covers that -
 but it is the manual's own worked example for this whole paragraph and
 belongs pinned alongside the fall-off cases it introduces.)

To score with a value called v.
  If v is a number, return a value, v.
  Otherwise, return a value, 99.

print score of 7.
print score of "hello".
